Measure fresh shared-frame acquisitions separately from host loop frequency.
Issue 31 reports severe stutter with ~54 guest FPS and 60 host Hz, but those
counters cannot detect repeated shared textures. Under existing GOW_PERF_DIAG
modes, emit bounded host-owned counters and hold age every five seconds.
No added GPU call, readback, fence wait or renderer behavior change.
Acquisitions are not changed-pixel counts, GPU time, scanout or input latency.
Validation and limitations: docs/research/issue-31-stutter-2026-11-09.md.

